Some vehicles roll off the lot with defects that never go away, no matter how many times you bring them in. If your car’s still under warranty and the problems won’t stop, you could be dealing with a lemon.

California’s lemon law was written to protect drivers in your exact situation. The Song-Beverly Consumer Warranty Act gives you the legal right to push back if the manufacturer can’t (or won’t) fix your vehicle. At [CLINE APC](/), our Glendale lemon law attorneys will go toe-to-toe with automakers to demand the refund, replacement, or payout you’re owed.

## Here’s When You May Have a Lemon Law Claim

- The dealership or manufacturer tried multiple times to fix the issue while the vehicle was still under warranty.

- Your car has spent 30 or more days in the shop for repairs related to covered defects.

- The defects aren’t the result of driver misuse, accidents, or lack of maintenance.

